WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.880
So let's get back to basics.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.730
It's not that simple.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.660
You really didn't see?

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.600
I didn't. And I forgot it!

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.270
If you forgot it,
you'll remember it later!

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.740
So what did you remember?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.390
Shut up, you!

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.140
Oh, it's been a while, Sasahara-sempai.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:19.960
Yo.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.010
Hello there.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.320
Oh, hello.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.440
Hello.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.220
So like I said, it's good to keep 
the existence of the reader in mind.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.030
The whole point is to share
 something with the reader, after all.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.400
Yes.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.030
But what you can't forget is that the
 author herself is the most important reader.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:43.040
If you don't think it's 
interesting, nobody else will.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:44.050
Yes.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.790
Sure, once a work is out there,
 it's not just yours anymore.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.100
T-This seems important.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:56.000
But until a work is written,
 nobody can even complain about it.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.000
That's right.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.930
Sempai's manga for <i>Afternoon</i>

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.240
got trashed by the online fans.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.690
Okay, I'm heading back to work now.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.470
You're still on the clock?

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.770
Oh, uh... I just came back to the 
club room to pick up a few things.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.060
Bye.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.110
Bye!

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.830
See you.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:19.850
Um...

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:22.950
I wanted to talk to him about my manga.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.870
So I had him come here. Don't worry about it.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.690
Anyway, we're here today to talk 
about our plans for the school fair.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.690
We're gonna cosplay again!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.030
The Cross-Dressing Way!

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.320
Survival Strategy!

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.390
Yes, we're doing it!
 So don't dress like that outside!

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.930
What are these outfits?

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.850
They're too into it.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.480
A special issue of
 <i>Mebaetame</i> for the school fair?

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.770
Yes, the topic can be the school fair.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:24.090
We'll use B5 paper, bigger than usual, 
with as many pages as we can manage.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.680
And sell it, right?

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.910
Yes.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.910
Um... are we allowed to sell it?

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:36.130
I think it'll be okay,
 but Genshiken's never done that.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.440
A club magazine at the school fair?

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:43.300
Hmm... I think a few of 
ours haven't been free.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.430
Last year we did a maid cafe, 
so we didn't draw anything.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.970
But when I was a freshman,
 I think we sold mags for about 100 yen.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.150
The Manga Club? I dunno.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.370
They probably haven't started anything yet.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.540
See ya.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.860
Of course you don't know.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.260
'Cause you got kicked out of that club!

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.170
For doing stuff with Ogi-sempai's circle.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.280
Comic Festival sealed your fate.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.960
I knew it was coming.
 And I feel good about it!

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.560
You should just join Genshiken!

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.250
Not happening. Ever.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.590
You should join a new circle too.
 Maybe Genshiken.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.140
Why are you laughing?

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.070
KOIBANA3

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.670
Looks like it's okay.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.430
Will this book just be 
manga and illustrations?

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:41.990
No. Text, pictures, whatever.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.630
Anything's okay.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.860
Maybe I'll write a story then!

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:46.490
What?

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:47.370
Ooh!

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.890
Are you a writer?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.180
Nope, never tried it.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.220
What?

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.440
But when I watch at you guys,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.510
it makes me want to create my own stuff too.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.600
I know! Let's make something 
together, Yajimacchi!

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.380
Huh?

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.140
I'll write a story, and you can do 
the illustrations! How about it?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.780
She's right. It might be better 
to make her take half the blame

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.290
than do something original, 
and embarrass myself alone!

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.070
Got any ideas?

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:18.880
Hmm... let me see.
 The topic's the school fair.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:21.480
A Warring States School Fair!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.220
I was an idiot to ask.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.160
What? Why? A school in the middle of its fair

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:29.490
is transported through time, building 
and all, into the middle of Sekigahara.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.800
It's super moe!

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.520
There's no point in having 
it be a school fair, then!

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.280
It could just be a normal high school!

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.810
The title, to me, suggests a school where 
all the warring states generals attend...

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:41.040
There's lots of those!

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.030
The theme could be one of a 
never-ending school fair...

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:47.080
I remember when I used to 
work on projects like that.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.760
I did it a lot in middle school.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.990
They usually don't work out, though.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.020
Good luck, guys!

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.190
What about you, Hato-kun?

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.100
Right!

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:00.540
If we put out a book,
 will you draw something for it?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.900
Um...

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:06.130
BL isn't allowed, right?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:10.550
As long as it's appropriate for 
all ages, some BL would be okay.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.760
Some... "some," is it?

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.730
Yes. From my perspective,
 the biggest mystery about Hato-kun

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.210
isn't her cross-dressing or 
love of BL. It's her art.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:25.660
Everything she draws for <i>Mebaetame</i> 
is BL in a shoujo manga style.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.650
It's all pro or better, and 
most of it is very extreme!

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:32.120
But when she was my assistant,

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.000
all the backgrounds she 
drew were very realistic.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.650
Hato-kun has the ability to switch styles,

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:41.660
and is skilled at both 
design and sketching.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.550
She must have a lot of experience 
drawing with a crow quill pen and ink.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:50.340
And yet, all I've seen from her are 
cuts and single illustrations.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.020
I've never seen her write a full manga.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:57.290
Maybe she hasn't written one?
 No, that's impossible.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.360
If she has, maybe she's better than me?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.270
Hato-kun...

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:04.820
Yes?

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:09.050
I'd really like to read a manga by you.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:28.440
I'm sorry. Can I think about it a little?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.530
Divide the page into panels.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.310
Sketch it out.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.660
Okay, this time...

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.890
Why does this always happen?

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.150
That's right.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:08.740
When you're dressed as a girl,
 you can only draw extreme BL scenes,

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.490
and when you're not,
 you can only draw <i>special</i> manga

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:14.840
about <i>special</i> characters.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:18.310
After what I said to Hato-kun...

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:21.260
I can't draw a thing.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:26.800
What?

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.810
"If you're tired, rest your head on my lap?"

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.170
I guess it couldn't hurt.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.930
What?

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:44.830
If you say anything embarrassing 
in your sleep, I'll punish you.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:48.540
Is that from some anime?

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:52.090
Like "Sasahara-san..."?

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:00.010
I'm sorry, I was kidding!
 I'd never say anything so embarrassing!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.980
You know I wouldn't!

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.980
Then change places...

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.130
Look at this quality research material!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.250
No way! I can't draw armor!

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:15.690
I'm sorry. It looks like writing 
a manga is going to be too hard.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:19.910
I see. What about
 Yoshitake-san and Yajima-san?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:24.780
We've broken up due to
 irreconcilable creative differences!

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.830
Her ideas are too stupid to draw.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:30.850
Why? The space samurai 
cavalry are the Eastern Army,

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.250
the school transforms into a super 
weapon for the Western Army,

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.830
and they fight at Osaka Castle!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.160
You just made that up to be a jerk!

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:38.530
You got stubborn and made the 
story even more ridiculous.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:44.440
Oh my! Does it look like the <i>Mebaetame 
School Fair Special</i> isn't happening?

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.780
Then why don't we just...

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.520
...all have a cosplay photo shoot!

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:49.520
We will not!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.980
Well, if all else fails,

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:56.590
I'm sure Ogi-sempai will 
write 50 pages by herself.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.430
Huh?

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:04.060
I-I was sure Hato-kun would draw something.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.000
Not happening, is it? Sorry.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.630
Um, to tell you the truth...

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.040
Your art changes...

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.590
...depending on how you're dressed?

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.000
Yes.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:22.510
When I'm a girl I can only 
draw really extreme stuff.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:27.230
Wait, wait, wait. When you were 
sempai's assistant you were a guy.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:31.500
I was just drawing
 backgrounds so it worked out.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.440
Do you have anything you drew as a guy?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:37.030
I did bring it, but...

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.470
It's really very different.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.950
<b>Where should I go?</b>

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.760
No way. You're joking.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:47.420
There's no way somebody 
drawing stuff like this

00:10:47.420 --> 00:10:50.370
could change just by putting 
on women's clothing.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:55.300
You're not wrong, but... it's true.

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.570
Before school started I was 
practicing cross-dressing.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:01.450
I decided to try and draw something, 
and it was like a limiter turned off.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.060
I suddenly was able to draw BL 
pictures like I was possessed.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:08.880
Um, I've heard of something 
causing a change in style,

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:13.480
or to get better...
 but changing that much...

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:18.150
Cross-dressing might be like some kind 
of self-hypnosis switch for her.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:19.780
Is that possible?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.210
When you look at Hato-kun, what do you think?

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:26.930
She's such a perfect girl that it feels 
like she's put herself under hypnosis.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.900
The cross-dressing and voice 
change are just a trigger.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:33.660
What makes her amazing 
is locked away inside.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.880
Maybe that's what transforms her

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.450
into the ideal rotten girl 
that she wants to be.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.110
Ideal rotten girl?

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:49.510
And it just so happens that part of that 
ideal is being good at drawing BL.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.240
I don't get it.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.960
So she tricks herself 
into being good?

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.690
Maybe.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:58.090
Come to think of it... even when she 
was asleep, she had a girl's voice.

00:11:58.090 --> 00:12:00.010
That isn't normal.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:07.240
But I just saw for sure that 
she's 100% a guy the other day.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.820
So how does this work?

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:15.760
You can't just draw a clean BL manga?

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.040
It's always just the dirty parts?

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.610
Yes. That's right.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:25.170
I forget myself and start 
ignoring the panel divisions.

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:29.850
That's not going to work.
 Let's all just cosplay instead.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.220
That's right!

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:33.850
E-Even if you're okay with 
that, I don't think...

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.580
N-n-n-n-nu-nu-PICCON!

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.730
What's that supposed to be?

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.450
You do the layouts.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:41.800
You draw the pictures.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.110
Huh?

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:45.070
Does that mean...

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.090
...we work together?

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:54.540
Um, freshmen girls...
 let me ask you some questions.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.100
When you were in high school,

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.000
did you ever fall in love?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.360
Huh?

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:03.010
Huh?!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:04.950
Wow, a twofer.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:10.290
Um... whether or not I do 
a manga with Hato-kun...

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.930
I wanted to try a different 
genre than I usually do,

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:17.920
and do a romance manga set 
at a high school culture fair.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:22.130
But I didn't do anything like 
that when I was in high school.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:25.050
I didn't even have any friends.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:28.110
You guys were high school 
students not that long ago,

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.950
so I'd like to hear if you have 
any love stories to tell me.

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:34.560
No, no, Ogi-sempai. I'm sorry, since 
everybody probably sees this coming,

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:39.300
but while I had passions 
in 2D and from history,

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:43.830
do you really think any of us have 
ever been in love? Right, Yajimacchi?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:48.170
Yeah... I guess so.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.720
Okay, Yajimacchi. DOUBT!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:52.860
What do you doubt?

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:54.820
Why are you being so indirect?

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.270
And you looked away too! It's obvious!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:01.120
I'll bring out my stash of the 
good snacks, so out with it!

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:04.350
Are we going to have a tea party? HTT?

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:07.900
If we leave it to Yoshitake-san, 
it'll probably work out.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.570
You really suck.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:15.130
You're an asshole. 
Who cares what you think?

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:20.060
No, no, that's Zora from <i>Ten 
Piece</i>. I really like him.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:23.750
<i>Ten Piece</i> is just too popular.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:26.810
I'm better. Gimme that pen.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:33.450
I win.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.170
I'm humiliated!

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:38.330
Well, I bet he practiced when he was a kid.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.730
Hey, you suck.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.440
You suck.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.820
Sucky!

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:51.580
Why do people call you "Sucky," Yajima?

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:53.050
I don't know!

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:00.440
I'm glad I ended up in 
your class again, Mirei.

00:15:01.390 --> 00:15:03.070
Yeah.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.240
I heard he's in class C.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.140
I went to the convienence store yesterday...

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.540
Hey, Yajima.

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:22.040
Bye.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:24.770
Yeah.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.790
That was our last conversation.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.280
No, no, Yajimacchi. Wait a second.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.520
What?

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:35.030
It's hard to say this, but...

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:39.730
Wasn't that just bullying?
"My classmates gave me a mean nickname!"

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.370
I thought so at the time.

00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:46.320
But he took it back in the end.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:52.030
What do you think of us, sempai?

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:55.140
Our bar for "romance" is set way too low!

00:15:56.140 --> 00:16:00.930
And what's worse, is even as far 
as Yajimacchi's lowered the bar,

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.890
I still can't clear it!

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.000
I spent every day in the history club,

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:09.230
getting into arguments about 
history, otaku, and BL!

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:12.910
So our last hope is Hato-chan!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.870
What's wrong, Hato-chan? You're bright red!

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.600
Am I?

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.850
Has there been anything in this 
story that'd make somebody blush?

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:23.800
What? What happened?

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:26.730
No. Either way, I mean...

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:30.880
I can't really help you... 
I've never dated anyone.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.800
And I've never even talked 
to anyone about it.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.140
When Yajima said, "He was 
better at drawing than me,"

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.140
she turned three times redder than normal!

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.560
Drawing?

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.150
Good eye, Sue-san!

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:45.250
What does that mean?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:49.320
It means something happened when 
Hato-chan was in high school.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.420
Does it have to do with drawing?

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:53.220
Ogi-sempai's taken the bait!

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:56.840
And Sue-san's got the snacks! 
She won't give them to anyone!

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:57.890
Nobody cares!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:01.110
Come on, Hato-chan, I'll give 
you this Godiver chocolate.

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:02.580
What? That looks expensive.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.780
You want it, Yajimacchi?

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:04.840
No, forget it.

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:07.000
Okay then. Here you go, Hato-chan.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:11.860
Um, well... when I was in high school...

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:13.560
High school?

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.800
That's right, when she was in high school...

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.790
Yeah, when you were in high school?

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:19.060
Wait, Yoshitake!

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:20.760
What?

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:23.500
Well, um...

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.690
You remember what happened when 
she was in high school, right?

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.790
We heard something bad happened, right?

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.420
When people found 
out she was into BL?

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:35.740
Yeah. When she came out about it 
in the art club, she got bullied.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:38.380
Yeah, that. So, well...

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:41.650
Let's not dig too deep into that, huh?

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:44.560
Oh, but I wanted to hear more about that too.

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:49.810
Would they really bully you 
just for being a guy into BL?

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:54.480
We found out about it the very first day,

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.770
and we didn't care.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:18:01.070
You were actually insistent 
that she come as a guy.

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:06.300
The first time I heard Hato's story, 
 I thought it was strange.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:09.970
Now, high school and college 
can be pretty different.

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:12.060
But I still thought to myself,

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:15.780
"I'm sure there's romance involved."

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.490
No... I don't think that was it.

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:24.640
Maybe the girls were fighting over 
you, and you didn't know about it.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.190
You're a cute guy too, Hato-chan,

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:31.110
so I wouldn't be surprised 
if you were popular.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:34.060
No, that wasn't true at all.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:37.800
I think the girls just 
thought I was pathetic.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.600
And the guys?

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.250
My guess is that there were 
guys fighting over you too,

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.740
and that's part of why you had trouble.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:50.520
What about you? You're always stylish, 
you had to have been popular!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.900
You don't get it, Hato-chan.

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:55.000
Huh?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.740
You don't dress stylishly or 
put on makeup to impress guys.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.090
You do it to keep other girls in their place.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:06.370
When you dress up, do you pay more 
attention to how girls or guys react?

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.020
You're right! I pay more 
attention to the girls!

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.610
Right? That's how it works.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:15.960
So why not tell me everything, huh?

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:18.800
It might help Ogi-sempai.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:19.490
Huh?

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:23.250
Oh, right. I was the one who brought this up.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:26.700
But I don't know about this.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.580
I thought I was bailing her out!

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:38.890
But I still...

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.700
...don't want to talk about it.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.220
Manabu!

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:51.180
Hey, everybody's here.
 Of course you are, it's a meeting!

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:54.960
So I've decided on my
 cosplay for the school fair.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:57.070
Tell Miss Tanaka for me.

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.400
I'll be a pair with Hato-chan.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.300
No cross-dressing for you.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:02.880
Why?

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:04.990
The trap phenomenon

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.340
is on the cutting edge of 
modern visual culture!

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:10.120
I can't deny that, but...

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.930
When you do it, it's just 
"creepy otaku" stuff.

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:15.650
People don't need more 
excuses to insult otaku.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.360
And Hato-kun's not cosplaying this time.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:19.240
Why?

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:22.270
Hato-kun is hiding her identity,

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:25.330
so she can't stand out while she's on campus.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:30.250
She can't show up as a guy, either, so 
she'll be cross-dressing in plain clothes.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.020
Yes.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.120
Give it up, please.

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:34.520
I-I can't believe it!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:37.460
By the way, Kucchi-sempai.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:41.110
Do you have any tales of 
romance from high school?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.490
I do.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.700
Ventura, Ventura--

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.310
Sempai?

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:52.480
W-W-Would you go out with me?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.410
<b>After Festival</b>

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:56.850
And so...

00:20:56.850 --> 00:21:00.600
some girl I didn't know asked me 
out in my last year of high school.

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:04.200
And we're done! If I hear this I won't 
be able to draw anything ever again!

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:07.330
We're doing standard anime-style manga!

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:08.830
Let's clean up.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:12.480
W-What's this? I sense a mood of disrespect.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:14.650
A very disrespectful mood!

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.160
That's weird. He wasn't trying, but...

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:20.110
...Kuchiki-sempai ended up saving me.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:23.950
So how long did you date her?

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.120
The next day she said, "Never mind."
 I spoke to her for less than three minutes.

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:13.350
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:13.320
Genshiken's publishing something 
for the school fair, aren't they?

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.820
With Ogiue there, of course they are!

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:20.160
I'm not sure about our postwar 
agricultural policies, either.

00:23:20.160 --> 00:23:22.980
Why are you here? You can't 
have my Giga Potato Chips!

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:25.290
If you can't eat, you get hungry!

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:27.280
Anything but rice would 
be less fuel-efficient.

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:29.220
Stop bringing back all these old jokes!

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:31.590
When you get hungry you get mad!

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:32.660
That's right.

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:35.140
Argh!

00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:39.470
Next time on <i>Genshiken: Second Generation</i>: 
There's a Route, but There's No Loop!
